      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and the single dose is also above the usual maximum. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
